Each curve traces the estimated probability of surviving past each time point. Subjects whose
covariates put them at higher risk drop faster. You can add custom labels with the `labels=`
parameter to make the legend more informative.

::: {#2882a6a1 .cell execution_count=43}
``` {.python .cell-code}
# Add descriptive labels to the predicted curves
gw.plot_predicted_survival(
    final,
    lung[cols][:4],
    labels=["Subject 1", "Subject 2", "Subject 3", "Subject 4"],
)
